- Use Ark address hints by default
  `Config::lightning_ark_address_hints` is now true by default. The wallet
  pays an invoice that carries an Ark address of its own Ark server with an
  arkoor, and asks for its Ark address in its invoices when the server allows
  it. Set it to false to pay every invoice over Lightning.
- Put the destination of a forwarded invoice in its route hints
  `Bolt11InvoiceBuilder::destination_hint` puts the claim destination in the
  route hints of the invoice, so a wallet on the same Ark server can pay the
  destination directly. A receive paid this way waits until the server reports
  the arkoor delivered to the destination, or settles right away when the
  server does not track delivery.
  - **BREAKING:** `Progress` of a Lightning receive has the variant
    `AwaitingDelivery`. An older wallet cannot read a receive in that state.
